{
  "_comment": [
    "English food term -> Bulgarian surface forms, injected into generic_foods.search_text",
    "by scripts/import-generic-foods.ts so a query in either language finds the same row.",
    "",
    "Keys are SINGULARIZED, lowercased English tokens — the output of tokenize() in",
    "src/services/fdc-text.ts. 'bananas' in a USDA description folds to 'banana', so that",
    "is the key. A key matching any token of a food's name contributes its Bulgarian forms.",
    "",
    "Values list every surface form worth matching, because search is substring-based:",
    "the haystack must literally contain what the user typed. Bulgarian inflects heavily,",
    "so singular AND plural are both listed ('банан' does not contain 'банани'). Definite",
    "forms ('бананът') are skipped — nobody types them into a search box, and the trigram",
    "similarity fallback catches them anyway.",
    "",
    "Culinary accuracy beats literal translation: olive oil is 'зехтин', not 'маслиново",
    "олио'; 'сирене' means white brine cheese, so cheddar is 'кашкавал'.",
    "",
    "Adding a term needs no migration — regenerate the seed and re-run the upsert."
  ],
